<div id="2026-09-10-model-upload-replace-stl" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-10 — Add STL upload/replace for print queue and model detail</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Added STL upload functionality so you can download a model's STL, modify it in a slicer, and upload the corrected version to replace it. New controller action <code>model_upload</code> at <code>POST /3d/model_upload/{model_id}</code> accepts a file upload, replaces the NFS file, preserves the model's DB record, re-parses STL volume/weight, and redirects back. Inline upload forms (hidden file input triggered by an "Upload New" / "Replace STL" label link) appear beside every download link on the print queue (<code>/3d/queue</code>), the printable queue view (<code>/3d/queue_print</code>), and the model detail page (<code>/3d/model</code>). The <code>queue_print.tt</code> template also gained download links (previously absent).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Inconsistent STL files were attached to models and there was no way to correct them from the queue. The user wanted to download a file, slice it with corrections, and upload the new version — all from the queue page without jumping to a separate model manager.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/3d.pm</code> (new <code>model_upload</code> action), <code>root/3d/queue.tt</code> (upload forms in queued/active/completed sections), <code>root/3d/queue_print.tt</code> (download+upload in all sections), <code>root/3d/model_detail.tt</code> (Replace STL button).</p>
</div>